    "q-31319": {
      "dom_id": "step-q31319",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$(r-2s)({r}^{2}+{s}^{2})=$",
      "worked_solution": "We take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-2s)({r}^{2}+{s}^{2}) & = \\\\ r({r}^{2}+{s}^{2})+(-2s)({r}^{2}+{s}^{2}) & = \\\\ {r}^{3}+r{s}^{2}-2s{r}^{2}-2{s}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot simplify the above expression any further because there are no like terms.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
